  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the dog as a symbol of marginalized group",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the dog in the image, which is being used as a metaphor for marginalized or undesirable people. The meme's text 'they did not even leave dogs' implies that the user (or the viewer) is identifying with the dog as a representation of a group that is excluded or dehumanized. This projection is implicit, as there are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the user is invited to see themselves in the role of the marginalized group symbolized by the dog.",
